{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1003483,"ns":0,"title":"Epistemic theories of truth","extract":"In philosophy and epistemology, epistemic theories of truth are attempts to analyze the notion of truth in terms of epistemic notions such as knowledge, belief, acceptance, verification, justification, and perspective. \nA variety of such conceptions can be classified into verificationist theories, perspectivist or relativist theories, and pragmatic theories.","description":"Attempts to analyze the concept of truth","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}